\section{Validation Protocol}
\label{sec:validation}

The validation of the AAAHSC--9.4 architecture is performed through a
multi-stage protocol designed to assess numerical stability, physical
consistency, cryptographic integrity, and multi-node scalability. Each
stage is executed independently and cross-verified to ensure that the
system satisfies the requirements of sovereign-grade relativistic
simulation.

\subsection{Stage I: Baseline Numerical Stability}
Baseline stability is evaluated by evolving a vacuum Schwarzschild
spacetime using the BSSN $3+1$ formulation across the full AMR hierarchy.
Metrics include:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Hamiltonian constraint norm $\|\mathcal{H}\|_2$,
    \item Momentum constraint norm $\|\mathcal{M}\|_2$,
    \item Gauge stability under $1+\log$ lapse and Gamma-driver shift,
    \item Absence of secular drift in curvature invariants.
\end{enumerate}
The simulation must maintain:
\begin{equation}
    \|\mathcal{H}\|_2, \|\mathcal{M}\|_2 \le 1.21 \times 10^{-13}.
\end{equation}

\subsection{Stage II: AMR Refinement Integrity}
AMR refinement is validated by inducing controlled curvature gradients and
verifying:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item correct triggering of refinement at $\theta \le 10^{-3}$,
    \item proper prolongation and restriction across levels,
    \item flux synchronization without numerical artifacts,
    \item GPU-resident execution of all boundary operations.
\end{enumerate}
Cross-level consistency is measured using:
\begin{equation}
    \Delta Q_{\ell,\ell+1} = 
    \left\| Q^{\ell} - \mathcal{R}(Q^{\ell+1}) \right\|_2.
\end{equation}

\subsection{Stage III: Semiclassical Backreaction Stability}
Hawking radiation source sinks are validated by evolving a near-horizon
region with semiclassical flux enabled. Stability criteria include:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item bounded negative-energy sink magnitude,
    \item monotonic horizon mass-loss rate,
    \item absence of curvature blow-up,
    \item consistent integration into $T_{\mu\nu}$.
\end{enumerate}
Mass-loss rate is compared against:
\begin{equation}
    \dot{M}_{\text{sim}} \approx \dot{M}_{\text{theory}}.
\end{equation}

\subsection{Stage IV: Secure Telemetry Ingestion}
Telemetry ingestion is validated using encrypted Gaia DR3 and LIGO O4
streams. Validation metrics include:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item correctness of lattice-based post-quantum decryption,
    \item preservation of data provenance,
    \item absence of injection-induced constraint drift,
    \item correct mapping of telemetry into boundary conditions.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Stage V: Multi-Node Scalability}
The Kubernetes/MPI topology is validated by deploying AAAHSC--9.4 across
heterogeneous GPU clusters. Metrics include:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item MPI domain decomposition consistency,
    \item non-blocking inter-node communication latency,
    \item AMR block placement stability under Kubernetes scheduling,
    \item linear or near-linear scaling with node count.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Stage VI: Cross-Regime Homeostasis}
The sovereign homeostasis controller is validated by evolving the system
through:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item weak-field regimes,
    \item strong-field regimes,
    \item near-horizon regimes,
    \item semiclassical evaporative regimes.
\end{enumerate}
Homeostasis is confirmed when:
\begin{equation}
    \frac{d}{dt} \|\mathcal{H}\|_2 \approx 0, \qquad
    \frac{d}{dt} \|\mathcal{M}\|_2 \approx 0.
\end{equation}

\section{Validation Summary}
The AAAHSC--9.4 architecture is considered validated when all stages
demonstrate numerical stability, physical consistency, cryptographic
integrity, and scalable multi-node performance without constraint drift
or refinement instability.